00:35:55.825 --> 00:35:58.098
But they were doing
natural experiments, and

00:35:58.099 --> 00:36:01.246
at the time these people hated
each other, they were fighting,

00:36:01.247 --> 00:36:03.520
and they were fighting
because the one group,

00:36:03.521 --> 00:36:06.120
the natural group was
like the epidemiologists.

00:36:06.121 --> 00:36:08.840
Well that is what they called
themselves to my knowledge, and

00:36:08.841 --> 00:36:09.800
then there was the other group,

00:36:09.801 --> 00:36:11.910
which was the we need
to prevent fraud group,

00:36:11.911 --> 00:36:14.541
both had totally legitimate
concerns, and so

00:36:14.542 --> 00:36:18.150
what ended up happening is this
guy Austin Bradford Hill said,

00:36:18.151 --> 00:36:19.960
why don't we just do both and
see if they match?

00:36:21.730 --> 00:36:24.370
And so what happened was they
come up with this concept called

00:36:24.371 --> 00:36:26.440
coherence, this is
Bradford Hill's big,

00:36:26.441 --> 00:36:30.270
big idea, like fundamentally
change the world.

00:36:30.271 --> 00:36:33.244
I don't mean that like in
a little way, it really did, and

00:36:33.245 --> 00:36:36.160
it led to what is now known as
the phase randomized control

00:36:36.161 --> 00:36:39.323
trial medicine, And eventually
something called Consort,

00:36:39.324 --> 00:36:42.606
which is an evidence standard to
show replication of studies and

00:36:42.607 --> 00:36:44.233
to diminish corporate fraud.

00:36:44.234 --> 00:36:45.715
So the idea was really simple,

00:36:45.716 --> 00:36:48.396
it's like if there's people
gathering natural data,

00:36:48.397 --> 00:36:51.150
why would we possibly not
wanna take that into account?

00:36:51.151 --> 00:36:54.210
On the other hand, since we know
that we can't control natural

00:36:54.211 --> 00:36:58.550
data, we should experimentation
at various scales, and

00:36:58.551 --> 00:37:00.650
the phased randomized control
trial allows for small and

00:37:00.651 --> 00:37:04.190
big ones, to root out who
the liars are, right?

00:37:04.191 --> 00:37:07.140
So it's a little bit of both,
you use a combination of

00:37:07.141 --> 00:37:10.460
metrics and you check
whether they agree or not.

00:37:10.461 --> 00:37:13.220
It turns out,
Christian's data on generics

00:37:13.221 --> 00:37:15.650
matches what other scholars
do in experimentation.

00:37:15.651 --> 00:37:17.999
You may not have known that,
